<title>INDIA: Indian soybean steady in dull trade, soymeal slips.</title>
<headline>Indian soybean steady in dull trade, soymeal slips.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1997-03-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Soybean prices were steady in central Indian markets on Wednesday, dealers said.</p>
<p>Arrivals were poor and volume was dull, they said.</p>
<p>Soybean market of Indore was closed to protest VAT (value added tax) imposed by the provincial government.</p>
<p>Edible oils market was also closed for the same reason.</p>
<p>Soymeal and rapeseed extraction prices fell on reduced export demand. Soymeal yellow was $304 per tonne FAS (free alongside ship) in bulk for export. Rapeseed extraction was $119-120 per tonne FAS in bulk for export. Rapeseed extraction was 4,050-4,100 rupees per tonne in FOR (free on rail).</p>
